---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import { u } from "../lib/url.js";
import plates from "../data/plates.json";
const REPO = "https://github.com/daviddef/TheFalco";
const registers = plates.filter(p => p.k === "register");
const photos = plates.filter(p => p.k !== "register");
---
<Base title="Documents">
  <h1>Documents</h1>
  <p class="lede">The images this archive actually rests on: the register pages that carry the
  evidence, and the family's own photographs. Every register plate below is reproduced with the
  archival reference that identifies it, so the claim and the page that proves it sit together.</p>

  <h2>Register pages</h2>
  <p>Reproduced from the Portale Antenati, which publishes the civil registers of the Archivio di
  Stato di Caserta. The transcription and translation of each is on the page linked beneath it.</p>

  {registers.map(p => (
    <figure class="plate">
      <img src={u("/plates/" + p.f)} alt={p.t} loading="lazy" />
      <figcaption>
        <h3>{p.t}</h3>
        {p.when ? <p class="small mono">{p.when}</p> : null}
        <p>{p.c}</p>
        <p class="small">{p.cite}</p>
        {p.see ? <p class="small"><a href={u(p.see)}>Read the act in full →</a></p> : null}
      </figcaption>
    </figure>
  ))}

  <h2>Photographs</h2>
  <p>From the family's own scans. <strong>Living people are omitted from this build</strong> — a
  further nineteen photographs in the family tree show living members and are not published here.
  That is a deliberate choice, not an oversight.</p>
  <div class="grid two">
    {photos.map(p => (
      <figure style="margin:0" class="card">
        <img src={u("/plates/" + p.f)} alt={p.t} loading="lazy"
             style="width:100%;height:auto;border-radius:.35rem;display:block" />
        <figcaption style="margin-top:.6rem">
          <strong>{p.t}</strong><br/><span class="small">{p.c}</span>
        </figcaption>
      </figure>
    ))}
  </div>

  <h2>The written record</h2>
  <p>Behind these images sit the files that carry every citation in the archive. They are plain
  tab-separated text, kept public so the working can be checked rather than trusted.</p>
  <ul>
    <li><a href={REPO + "/blob/main/data/record-citations.tsv"}>record-citations.tsv</a> — every
    record citation, with its archival reference.</li>
    <li><a href={REPO + "/blob/main/data/households.tsv"}>households.tsv</a> — every register entry
    behind the households, quoted in the words of the record.</li>
    <li><a href={REPO + "/blob/main/data/direct-line.tsv"}>direct-line.tsv</a> — the generations, and
    the evidence for each join.</li>
  </ul>
  <p class="small">The page-by-page reading logs for the civil death registers —
  <a href={REPO + "/blob/main/notes/1833-death-register-progress.md"}>1833</a>,
  <a href={REPO + "/blob/main/notes/1834-death-register-progress.md"}>1834</a>,
  <a href={REPO + "/blob/main/notes/1835-death-register-progress.md"}>1835</a>,
  <a href={REPO + "/blob/main/notes/1836-death-register-progress.md"}>1836</a> — record every act
  read, not only the ones that mattered, so that nobody has to read them again.
  Full list of sources on the <a href={u("/sources")}>Sources</a> page.</p>
</Base>
